Room: Room's TabDialogs for a tab.

Room asks the host when a page stops responding (instead of Chrome's hung
renderer dialog) and routes the password manager's automatic offers to the
host (3.7a, 4.x). Until 156 //room swapped the page's TabDialogs, a
WebContents user data. 157 made TabDialogs a member of the tab's
TabFeatures, created by TabDialogs::Create and registered on the tab's
unowned user data: there is nothing left to swap. A factory redirect gives
TabDialogs::Create Room's subclass of TabDialogsViews; everything it does
not answer stays Chrome's.

Phase 6.4 (the rebase to 157), 2026-11-02. //room: room/core/room_page_dialogs.mm.
diff --git a/chrome/browser/ui/views/tab_dialogs_views.cc b/chrome/browser/ui/views/tab_dialogs_views.cc
index d85a7322ba380..8b9221b96889a 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/views/tab_dialogs_views.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/views/tab_dialogs_views.cc
@@ -19,10 +19,21 @@
 #include "chrome/browser/ui/views/web_apps/force_installed_preinstalled_deprecated_app_dialog_view.h"
 #endif
 
+namespace room {
+// Room: set by //room/core at startup. A TabDialogsViews of Room's for every
+// tab (the hung-page question and password offers go to the host).
+std::unique_ptr<TabDialogs> (*g_create_tab_dialogs_hook)(tabs::TabInterface&,
+                                                         content::WebContents*) =
+    nullptr;
+}  // namespace room
+
 // static
 std::unique_ptr<TabDialogs> TabDialogs::Create(tabs::TabInterface& tab,
                                                content::WebContents* contents) {
   DCHECK(contents);
+  if (room::g_create_tab_dialogs_hook) {
+    return room::g_create_tab_dialogs_hook(tab, contents);
+  }
   return std::make_unique<TabDialogsViews>(tab, contents);
 }
 
